timeline.body:
Since the Containers/Metrics API in the JDK is Linux only[1] and the non-Linux impls do nothing, I'd add native linkage for Linux only use as well. Something like this?

```
diff --git a/substratevm/src/com.oracle.svm.core/src/com/oracle/svm/core/jdk/PlatformNativeLibrarySupport.java b/substratevm/src/com.oracle.svm.core/src/com/oracle/svm/core/jdk/PlatformNativeLibrarySupport.java
index 7a7162a58512..799e42fe0c5b 100644
--- a/substratevm/src/com.oracle.svm.core/src/com/oracle/svm/core/jdk/PlatformNativeLibrarySupport.java
+++ b/substratevm/src/com.oracle.svm.core/src/com/oracle/svm/core/jdk/PlatformNativeLibrarySupport.java
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@ public abstract class PlatformNativeLibrarySupport {
         builtInPkgNatives = new ArrayList<>();
         if (Platform.includedIn(InternalPlatform.PLATFORM_JNI.class)) {
             builtInPkgNatives.addAll(Arrays.asList(defaultBuiltInPkgNatives));
+            /* Containers and Metrics internal API is Linux only */
+            if (Platform.includedIn(InternalPlatform.LINUX.class)) {
+                 builtInPkgNatives.add("jdk_internal_platform");
+            }
         }
     }
```

[1]
```
$ find src/java.base/share/classes/jdk/internal/platform/
src/java.base/share/classes/jdk/internal/platform/
src/java.base/share/classes/jdk/internal/platform/Metrics.java
src/java.base/share/classes/jdk/internal/platform/Container.java
```

